      <title>Episode 3: 'Against the Ruck' - A History of Black Rugby - Jacana</title>
      <link>https://jacana.co.za/episode-3-against-the-ruck-a-history-of-black-rugby/</link>
      <description>A compelling new book, ‘Rugby, Resistance and Politics’, by historian Buntu Siwisa takes us back to the roots of black rugby back in the 1820s, and tells Charles Leonard in this episode of Sound of Jacana podcast why rugby is far more popular than football in black communities of the Eastern Cape.</description>
